          "No direct control over company operations"
        ],
        [
          "Nature of Capital",
          "Long-term, stable capital flow",
          "Short-term, volatile 'hot money'"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "xx1gao9"
    },
    {
      "id": "gut3j6b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "18. Appreciation (Currency)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vjx75ne",
      "content": "Rise in value of domestic currency."
    },
    {
      "id": "pjxa3tr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "19. FDI (Foreign Direct Investment)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ej2dmbi",
      "content": "Long-term foreign investment with management control."
    },
    {
      "id": "ltq3695",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "20. FPI (Foreign Portfolio Investment)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xi745b6",
      "content": "Investment in financial assets without control."
    },
    {
      "id": "5ctgb9i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "21. Human Development Index (HDI)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "36z28gb",
      "content": "Composite index measuring health, education and income."
    },
    {
      "id": "ejmjv98",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "22. Poverty Line"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6x8ed19",
      "content": "Minimum income required to meet basic needs."
    },
    {
      "id": "r9eo2i5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "23. Multiplier Effect"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "271h4wc",
      "content": "Increase in income resulting from increase in government spending."
    },
    {
      "id": "vn67sq6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "24. Subsidy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wulhua8",
      "content": "Financial assistance given by government to reduce cost of goods/services."
    },
    {
      "id": "g4rwtx9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "25. Public Debt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jr8a8rl",
      "content": "Total borrowings of the government."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Repo Rate is the interest rate at which RBI lends short-term money to commercial banks, whereas Reverse Repo Rate is the rate at which RBI borrows from banks.",
        "Direct Tax burden cannot be shifted (e.g., Income Tax), while Indirect Tax burden is passed to the final consumer (e.g., GST).",
        "FDI involves direct ownership of physical assets and active management, whereas FPI involves passive investment in financial securities like shares and bonds."
      ],
      "id": "7pajn82"
    },
    {
      "id": "6t6ncrx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "26. Tax Buoyancy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lxg6sio",
      "content": "Responsiveness of tax revenue to changes in GDP."
    },
    {
      "id": "6n82du7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "27. Capital Account"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
